<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · infrastructure</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lines of Torres Vedras</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1809">1809</a>–<a href="/years/1810">1810</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Lines of Torres Vedras were lines of forts and earthworks built in secret in 1809–1810 on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wellington">Wellington</a>'s orders to defend <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lisbon">Lisbon</a> during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peninsular-war">Peninsular War</a>. Stretching across the peninsula north of the city, they stopped Marshal Masséna's French army in October 1810. Unable to break through and starving in a stripped countryside, the French withdrew from Portugal in 1811.</p></div>
